Three LEDs (D13, D12, D11) start off. Only the second button on D3 is pressed, so kod = 2. Which LEDs stay lit when this program runs?

```
switch (kod) {
  case 1:
    digitalWrite(13, HIGH);
    break;
  case 2:
    digitalWrite(12, HIGH);
  case 3:
    digitalWrite(11, HIGH);
    break;
}
```

The button is between D2 and GND (INPUT_PULLUP). Even when you press the button, the LED never lights. Which line is wrong?

```
int durum = digitalRead(2);
if (durum = LOW) {
  digitalWrite(13, HIGH);
} else {
  digitalWrite(13, LOW);
}
```

